# Witness: a legend that publishes one of the nine twice

Set equality alone does not see this: the nine are all published and no tenth is added. A
legend that lists `[MET]` twice is still a legend that has been edited without being read, and
the duplicate clause is the only thing that reports it.

## 1. How To Use This File

### Evidence verdicts - set by the author, about evidence

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[MET]` | Demonstrated. |
| `[MET]` | Demonstrated, said a second time. |
| `[PART]` | Partly demonstrated. |
| `[UNMET]` | Not discharged. |
| `[N/A]` | Not claimed at this milestone. |

### Review verdicts - set by the reviewer, about their own reading

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[ ]` | Not yet reviewed. |
| `[A]` | Accepted as stated. |
| `[C]` | Accepted with a condition. |
| `[R]` | Rejected. |
| `[?]` | Cannot be judged from what is here. |
